[{:db/id 17592186124485 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0c07b7ca-2c8b-5a74-a857-c6a369e5fb28"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0c07b7ca-2c8b-5a74-a857-c6a369e5fb28" :question/id #uuid "0c07b7ca-2c8b-5a74-a857-c6a369e5fb28" :question/math-academy-id "q-35580" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly dependent and ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$\n- ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$\n- ${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, solving equation ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ for ${v}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=-\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{3}-\\frac{{x}_{4}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nMoreover, ${x}_{2}$ can't be zero because then\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nwill have a non-zero solution and that's a contradiction as ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent.\nHence, ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent set, the equation \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3}+{x}_{3}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas no non-zero solution. Hence, ${v}_{4}$ is not a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f0e50222-5322-5dc6-95c0-87aed25c41a3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f0e50222-5322-5dc6-95c0-87aed25c41a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0e50222-5322-5dc6-95c0-87aed25c41a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7b430210-150a-5113-bb9e-9ceedc527951" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1688faeb-85ba-5d68-81e7-78a4a337f227" "answer-f381c62f-1e63-5006-ba9d-a84a80c6800c" "answer-888ec5b1-c2ea-5a99-8c7a-f1ea5fd2dbc6" "answer-7b430210-150a-5113-bb9e-9ceedc527951" "answer-a66c38ea-8581-5edc-9742-8946b8e3e270"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1688faeb-85ba-5d68-81e7-78a4a337f227" :answer/id #uuid "1688faeb-85ba-5d68-81e7-78a4a337f227" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f381c62f-1e63-5006-ba9d-a84a80c6800c" :answer/id #uuid "f381c62f-1e63-5006-ba9d-a84a80c6800c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-888ec5b1-c2ea-5a99-8c7a-f1ea5fd2dbc6" :answer/id #uuid "888ec5b1-c2ea-5a99-8c7a-f1ea5fd2dbc6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b430210-150a-5113-bb9e-9ceedc527951" :answer/id #uuid "7b430210-150a-5113-bb9e-9ceedc527951" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a66c38ea-8581-5edc-9742-8946b8e3e270" :answer/id #uuid "a66c38ea-8581-5edc-9742-8946b8e3e270" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a20e067c-d0eb-5b47-b6b0-79dbc97af27c" :activity/id #uuid "a20e067c-d0eb-5b47-b6b0-79dbc97af27c" :activity/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048257 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity